  "notes": "**Hutsix v3.3.0**(released)\n\n### Running Profiles\n- The Run Profile status line now says **why** a profile is paused \u2014 for example `Active: Lol (paused: target window not focused)` \u2014 instead of only that it is paused. A profile that pauses without saying why looks exactly like a broken one.\n- A profile no longer stays silently paused after you stop and restart it. **Auto Pause On Focus Loss** could leave a pause behind that outlived the profile it belonged to, so afterwards no hotkey or other trigger fired while the window still showed the profile as running. The pause now belongs to the watcher that set it and is released whenever that profile stops \u2014 from the button, the tray, the abort hotkey or the auto-activator \u2014 and the profile also reports itself as paused while it really is.\n\n### Updates\n- **Resolved: release notes showed raw markdown.** The **What's new** list in the update prompt is formatted now: headings, bold text and bullet lists look like text instead of showing the raw `##`, `###` and `**` markers copied out of the release-notes file.\n- **Resolved: a paragraph that began with bold text was drawn as a bullet** with its first asterisk eaten. This also affected the Help and Tips & Tricks windows.\n\n### Bindings\n- **Cooldown now applies to hotkey triggers.** When a binding's repeat mode is **Cooldown**, pressing its key or mouse button again inside the cooldown does nothing \u2014 before, every press fired regardless of the value you had set (a 5-second cooldown could fire twice in two seconds). Repeated holds still re-fire at the cooldown interval, and the key or click still reaches the game instead of being swallowed. Interval-mode bindings behave exactly as before, and **0** still means \"no cooldown\".",
